/**

 @page benchmarks_swift2_hydro_noh_celldepth_test_2D 2D Noh implosion celldepth test

 Simple Noh implosion test benchmark in 2D with @f$ N ^d @f$ particles.
 This benchmark uses the same initial conditions setup for the physics as
 @ref benchmarks_swift2_hydro_noh_implosion_test_2D. However, here we benchmark
 how the code performs depending on minimal and maximal cell sizes (and hence
 also tree depths) for a range of @f$ N @f$ particles per dimension.


 As with all Swift 2 experiments, you have to ensure that you translate with
 ```--enable-particles --enable-swift``` before you start working with the
 scripts. Furthermore, either install the peano4 python package locally:

 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 pip3 install -e /path/to/Peano
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 or manually set the Python path (discouraged):

 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 export PYTHONPATH=~/../../../../python
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 The provided scripts in this directory will set up the experiments for you.
 Use

 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 ./build_celldepth_test_execs.sh
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 to compile a range of executables for varying cell min/max sizes and particle
 numbers. Then use


 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 ./run_celldepth_test.sh
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 to run them sequentially, or help yourself to the job scripts in the
 ```jobscripts``` subdirectory.


 Finally, you can plot the outcomes using

 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 python3 ./plot_celldepth_benchmarks.py
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 use the ```--help``` flag to see available plotting options.
 By default, the script will read in all available logfiles and plot them.
 See the header of the script for more details on the output format and usage.

 */
